From b29a49d27fb6745e312d364776d1112db51d3b5f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (for Kush)" <kushisthecoolest@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:18:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] remixbridge: POSIX port (libremixbridge.so)

All Windows code stays as it was, behind #ifdef _WIN32. On other
platforms:

- The runtime is loaded with dlopen(RTLD_NOW | RTLD_LOCAL) and dlsym.
  Paths from Java go through UTF-16, not modified UTF-8. remixapi_Path
  is wchar_t (UTF-32) for CreateTextureFromFile.
- A fatal-signal handler (SIGSEGV, SIGBUS, SIGILL, SIGFPE, SIGABRT)
  replaces the unhandled-exception filter and minidump. It writes
  crash/crash_report_<time>.txt (signal, fault address, module,
  registers, faulting-thread backtrace, /proc/self/maps) and chains to
  the previous handler, normally the JVM's. Faults in JIT code or
  libjvm (implicit null checks, safepoints) are passed straight on.
- No Toolhelp: other threads are not walked. The JVM's hs_err log
  lists them.
- Tracy symbols are looked up with dlsym in the loaded runtime.
- The command line is presented from the kernel's argument area
  (/proc/self/stat arg_start/arg_end) with CommandLineToArgvW quoting.
  Redaction blanks the source bytes, so /proc/<pid>/cmdline no longer
  shows the values.
- Present always passes PresentInfo: there is no window handle, and the
  headless runtime needs skipVulkanSwapchain and the interop fields.
- GL semaphore entry points are resolved through glXGetProcAddressARB,
  then eglGetProcAddress, from the libraries LWJGL already loaded.
- D3D9 helpers use DXVK native's type widths. Release is called
  through vtable slot 2.

remix_c.h takes the runtime's POSIX header block, which changes nothing
on Windows. CMakeLists.txt builds build/native/linux64/libremixbridge.so;
build_native.bat is unchanged.

